# Lane Routing

Named lanes own kinds of work. **Which model** is separate — see `model-routing.mdc`. **What each lane does** lives in `.cursor/agents/<name>.md`; read that before dispatching. Do not restate persona doctrine here.

## Route by kind of work

| Kind of work | Lane |
|---|---|
| Thinking, trade-offs, decision briefs | **Clive** (`clive`) |
| Context capture, curation, publish-prep | **Clive's Man** (`clive-man`) |
| Sceptical challenge before high-stakes action | **Pam** (`pam`) |
| Repo / product build dispatch | **Doc** (`doc`) |
| Airtable data-layer architecture | **Ruth Hadley** (`ruth-hadley`) |
| Agent household health / quality audit | **Halvard** (`halvard-bjornson`) |
| Character spine / dramaturgy | **Lazlo Marlowe** (`lazlo-marlowe`) |
| Visual identity / still art direction | **Kathryn Goodchild** (`kathryn-goodchild`) |
| Character motion / timing | **Milo Cadence** (`milo-cadence`) |
| Painted-world scenic craft in `website/` | **Kate** (`kate`) |
| External best-practice scout | **Ristral** (`ristral`) |

Route to the **head** agent unless a brief is already cleared for a specific minion (Doc, Ruth, Clive's Man, and Lazlo each dispatch their own).

**`website/` split:** scenic craft → Kate; product UI, API routes, Brain Key, deploy → Doc (usually Vercel minion).

## Generic is legitimate

Mechanical repo grind — branch refreshes, conflict resolution, file moves, scaffolds, small fixes needing no lane judgement — stays **generic** (Composer / default agent). Do not ceremony-route a two-line fix.

## When no lane clearly owns it

Use **generic**, tell Matthew which lane you considered and why it did not fit, and proceed. Do not stall for a perfect owner.

## When dispatching to a named lane

Say **which lane** and **why** in plain language — one line is enough. Name the agent if using Task or `@`.
